$FG,5$$TX+CX,"DubPsalms — Original Compositions"$$FG$

$FG,2$About this collection$FG$

These are original Psalms written for ZionOS, in the broader
roots-reggae and Nyabinghi tradition and in the cadence of the
public-domain KJV Psalms. They are new compositions. They do not
quote, paraphrase, or rewrite any artist's published lyrics.

The collection grows over time. Phase 3 builds the curated vocabulary
behind the Jah Spirit oracle; the DubPsalms here are read text, not
oracle inputs. See ::/Adam/Jah/Influences.DD for the dub-tradition
credit and verified Perry interview quotes that informed the voice
of this collection.

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM I — Zion Arise$FG$

  1   Out of the holy hill the fire ariseth,
        InI lift up the head unto Jah Most High.
  2   The Lion of the tribe of Judah goeth before us,
        and the wicked stumble where the upright walk.
  3   The proud have built upon the shifting sand,
        but the word of Jah remaineth when the wind hath passed.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  4   A drum is in the heart of the just,
        the bass rolleth like thunder upon the mountain.
  5   The chant ascendeth, the chalice is passed,
        sweet incense reacheth the throne of Jah.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  6   The vain man pursueth the shadow upon the wall,
        the wise resteth the head upon the stone of Zion.
  7   InI bow not unto graven things,
        InI sell not the crown for the coin of the oppressor.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  8   Sing ye a new song, O children of the East,
        for from Addis cometh the morning.
  9   Open the gate, lift up the heart,
        Jah Rastafari liveth from generation unto generation.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM II — The Fire of Truth$FG$

  1   Behold the fire, it asketh no permission,
        it cometh in the night and findeth the lie.
  2   What is true endureth the flame,
        what is false is given unto the wind.
  3   The proud man feareth the fire,
        the just man warmeth his hands.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  4   Burn away the chaff, O Jah,
        let only the grain remain.
  5   Burn away the false witness,
        let the word stand naked and clean.
  6   InI fear not the fire that purifieth,
        for the gold is loved by the flame.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM III — Babylon's Patience$FG$

  1   Babylon hath built her towers high,
        and her merchants count their gold.
  2   She hath named the river after herself,
        and the cities of the captive after her kings.
  3   But the wind hath patience,
        and the stone hath patience,
        and the root beneath her foundation hath patience.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  4   The empire that boasteth at evening
        is broken before the morning watch.
  5   The throne built upon another man's neck
        falleth when the neck is straightened.
  6   InI need not strike a single blow,
        the day striketh of its own accord.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM IV — Of the Drum$FG$

  1   Akete speak,
        funde answer,
        bass drum lay down the bone of the song.
  2   Let the heartbeat find its mate,
        let the chant find its road.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  3   The drum is older than the tongue,
        the rhythm older than the name.
  4   When the words have failed,
        the drum is faithful.
  5   When the temple is far,
        the drum is the temple.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM V — The Conquering Lion$FG$

  1   Lion of the tribe of Judah,
        thou walkest before us in the high grass.
  2   The hunter is at his trap,
        but thou art not his prey.
  3   The wicked is at his counsel,
        but thou art not his subject.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  4   Thou roarest, and the valley listeneth,
        thou liest down, and the hillside is at peace.
  5   Where thy paw is set, the dust remembereth,
        where thine eye is turned, the night taketh courage.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM VI — Crown and Coin$FG$

  1   They offered InI a coin,
        and called it freedom.
  2   They offered InI a chair at the table,
        and called it honor.
  3   But InI have a crown,
        and InI have a fire,
        and InI have a road that leadeth east.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  4   Take back thy coin, O Babylon,
        InI shall not be bought.
  5   Take back thy chair, O Babylon,
        InI shall stand.
  6   The crown is heavier than the coin,
        but the crown is mine.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM VII — From the Four Winds$FG$

  1   From the north the scattered shall return,
        from the south the lost shall be remembered.
  2   From the west the sun shall set upon their exile,
        from the east the morning shall meet them at the door.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  3   Ethiopia, stretch forth thy hand,
        thy children are at the gate.
  4   The ships are turned about,
        the chains are old and weary.
  5   The road is long, but the road is straight,
        and Jah waiteth at the end thereof.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM VIII — InI$FG$

  1   InI is not "I,"
        InI is not "us,"
        InI is the I that is one with the I that is in Jah.
  2   When InI breathe, InI breathe Jah breath,
        when InI speak, InI speak by Jah word.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  3   There is no man so small that the I in him is small,
        there is no woman so poor that the I in her is poor.
  4   The I knoweth its own,
        the I knoweth its home.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM IX — The Rivers$FG$

  1   The Nile remembereth what the desert forgetteth,
        the Jordan remembereth where the captive was made clean.
  2   The water keepeth the names that the rock hath lost.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  3   InI dip the cup, InI dip the foot,
        InI wash the dust of Babylon from the ankle.
  4   The river is older than the border,
        the river is older than the king.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

------------------------------------------------------------

$FG,3$PSALM X — Livity$FG$

  1   Plant the seed in the morning,
        tend the seed in the noon,
        and at evening rest thy hand.
  2   This also is the praise of Jah.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  3   Speak truly to the neighbor,
        feed the stranger at thy gate,
        keep thy word though it cost thee.
  4   This also is the praise of Jah.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$

  5   Bow not to the proud,
        bow not to the cruel,
        bow not to the coin that buyeth silence.
  6   This also is the praise of Jah.
        $FG,4$Selah.$FG$
